.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=Contents
.Options CtrlStartPosChar=^<wrap>

@Contents
$^#PaneFilter ${PLUGIN_VERSION}#
$^#Contents#

PaneFilter opens a FAR plugin panel backed by the current directory.
It can be started from the plugins menu, from a macro, or from the
command line with the #panefilter:# prefix (for example #panefilter:*.txt#).

Type to filter the panel contents.
Matching is case-insensitive.
If the filter contains #*# or #?#, wildcard matching is used.
#Alt+-# also types #*#.
Characters that would leave the panel empty are ignored.

#Enter#
Close PaneFilter and act in the real panel.
Directories change the real panel directory.
Files are positioned in the real panel and opened as if Enter was pressed there.

#Backspace#
Delete the last character from the filter.
If the filter becomes empty, PaneFilter closes and returns to the original item.

#Del#
Close PaneFilter and jump to the currently selected item in the real panel.
If the filter is already empty, PaneFilter closes and returns to the original item.

#Ctrl-R#
Refresh the directory contents.

#Esc#
Close PaneFilter and return to the original directory and item.

Other FAR file operations (F3, F4, F5, F6, F8, ...) work on the real files;
the panel is rescanned afterwards.
